cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "RASH-HIT Fractal Analysis"
abstract: "A research-grade, zero-rasterization computational geometry engine for exact vector box-counting, spatial occupancy profiling (fill vs. empty void ratio), and fractal dimension (Db) analysis directly from SVG vector motifs, architectural drawings, and textile patterns. Two measure modes: the default exact vector-geometry AREA engine (visual fill including stroke width via Shapely/GEOS, vendored 1:1 from RASH-HIT Fraktal Studio) and the legacy pure NumPy supercover segment engine on a fixed-point integer lattice (geometric-contact semantics, touch_counts boundary policy)."
version: "1.3.0"
date-released: "2026-10-21"
license: "Apache-2.0"
